  "experimental_conditions": {
    "001": {
      "0": {
        "detector": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(MAGSP,SI,TELES)",
            "free_txt": [
              " The SOLARIS solenoidal spectrometer",
              "with a magnetic field of 3 T. HELIOS four-sided array",
              "of position-sensitive silicon detectors (PSD)."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "facility": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(LINAC,1USAMSU)",
            "free_txt": [
              " The ReA6 reaccelerator-beam facility",
              "of the National Superconducting Cyclotron Laboratory",
              " (NSCL)."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "inc-spect": [
          {
            "x4_code": null,
            "free_txt": [
              "32Si beam, a long-lived radioisotope, had an",
              "intensity of approximately 10**5 particles per second",
              "and a beam purity of ~90% due to a 32S contaminant."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "method": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(EDE,COINC)",
            "free_txt": [
              " Protons produced by reactions of the 32Si",
              "beam impinging on (CD2) n target were analyzed by the",
              "newly developed SOLARIS solenoidal spectrometer. The",
              "energies and positions at which the protons returned",
              "to the beam axis were measured using the HELIOS",
              "array. The projectile-like Si recoils were uniquely",
              "identified from other reaction channels or un-reacted",
              "beam components, including the 32S contaminant, by a",
              "square (5x5 cm2) Si recoil detector telescope with",
              "quadrant segmentation in the dE. A 20-ns timing",
              "coincidence between the protons and the Si recoils",
              "was applied to select the (d,p) reaction channel, to",
              "separate the S contamination and to reduce the",
              "background."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sample": [
          {
            "x4_code": null,
            "free_txt": [
              "A 120-microg/cm2 (CD2)n target."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "status": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(APRVD)",
            "free_txt": [
              " Approved by J.Chen on October 10, 2025."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "002": {
      "0": {
        "err-analys": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(DATA-ERR)",
            "free_txt": [
              " The uncertainties of the absolute cross",
              "sections are estimated to be around 30-50%, which is",
              "dominated by the estimated uncertainty in the angular",
              "coverage of the recoil detectors."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "status": [
          {
            "x4_code": "(TABLE,,J.Chen+,J,PL/B,853,138678,2024)",
            "free_txt": [
              " Fig. 2",
              "Data were provided by J.Chen on 10/9/2025."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "003": {
      "0": {
        "analysis": [
          {
            "x4_code": null,
            "free_txt": [
              "Distorted-wave Born approximation (DWBA) calculations",
              "were performed with the code PTOLEMY. For the four",
              "lowest-lying states, the agreement between the",
              "experimental angular distributions and the DWBA",
              "calculation confirms previous momentum assignments.",
              "For the unbound states, a binding energy of 200 keV",
              "for the transferred neutron was assumed in a",
              "\"quasi-bound\" approach. The 4.52(4)- and 5.43(4)-MeV",
              "resonances have fitted widths Gamma = 220(80) keV and",
              "Gamma < 90 keV, and were tentatively assigned l = 1,2",
              "and l = 3, respectively."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "err-analys": [
